[38;5;231m⏺[39m Done. TLS verification stays on for both environments.

  [1m[38;5;153mclient.py[0m — added a module-level [38;5;153mVERIFY[39m read from [38;5;153mREPORTS_CA_BUNDLE[39m, defaulting to [38;5;153mTrue[39m, and passed it to both
  [38;5;153mrequests.get[39m calls. [38;5;153mrequests[39m takes either [38;5;153mTrue[39m (system trust store) or a CA bundle path, so staging's self-signed cert
  gets a trust anchor instead of an opt-out. [38;5;153mexport_prod.py[39m sets no bundle, so the nightly production export keeps
  default verification.

  [1m[38;5;153mscripts/sync_staging.py[0m — sets [38;5;153mREPORTS_CA_BUNDLE[39m via [38;5;153msetdefault[39m, so an exported value wins.

  Two things to check:

